THE INVARIANT THIS EXISTS TO PROTECT
Portfolio totals are SUMMED from the per-property schedules, never
recomputed from source data. The pack shows both views; if the portfolio
figure were derived independently the two could disagree, and an
accountant reconciling them would have no way to tell which was right.
Tested directly: portfolio net == sum of property nets == gross rent less
total deductions, and the summed deduction LINES also reconcile with the
summed property totals.

OTHER BEHAVIOUR
- Excluded properties (primary residence) are carried through with their
  reason rather than dropped, so every property the owner holds is
  accounted for. They contribute to no total, including cost base.
- Cost base is carried per property and totalled; it is not a rental
  schedule figure and stays separate from the income/deduction identity.
- propertiesAtLoss is reported separately from the portfolio result: a
  portfolio can be net positive while individual properties are negatively
  geared, and the accountant needs both.
- Deduction lines are summed into COPIES. The first occurrence is spread
  into a new object before accumulation, so aggregating a schedule does not
  mutate it. A test aggregates the SAME schedule object twice and asserts
  the source line is unchanged - without the copy this silently corrupts
  the per-property view the pack also prints.

